title: 'Gnomon session 2026-10-18/19: Mac daily-driver build, guided onboarding, Orca audit; process hardening started'
summary: |-
  Merged to feat/gnomon, with CI green at each merge:
  - M1.13 wrapper app;
  - M1.11 slice 3 mods;
  - P8-D97 repo context and its F1–F4 follow-ups;
  - bare `gnomon` and the installer;
  - guided first-run onboarding (MVP-a: Provisioner, preflight, `gnomon setup --cli`; MVP-b: setup endpoint, GUI screens, wrapper Phase::Setup, helper 1.4.0 presence.available);
  - the Linux lock-nonce fix;
  - the Chrome WebSocket Sec-Fetch-Site fix (the first dogfood run showed a blank page);
  - auto-open in the default browser through osascript stdin.
  Founder rulings:
  - every setup step needs a guided UI, and the CLI stays as the raw form;
  - the founder waits for the full experience before testing;
  - gnomon must open the browser seamlessly.
  The Orca audit produced the adopt list T-009 (now in progress on gnomon/process-hardening) and the spec decisions T-010.
  Founder status: the hardware test passed; guided setup is not yet run (the next step).
symbols_touched:
  - '#gnomon-wrapper'
  - '#bare-entry'
  - '#provisioner'
  - '#first-run'
  - '#setup-endpoint'
  - '#gui-setup'
  - '#web-endpoint'
  - '#supervisor'
  - '#session-runner'
decisions:
  - id: D-ui-first
    decision: Every user-facing setup step gets a guided UI; the CLI verbs remain as the raw form
    rationale: 'Founder: the tool needs proper UI/UX for everyone'
  - id: D-auto-open
    decision: gnomon auto-opens the default browser via osascript stdin (the URL is never on argv); --no-open and GNOMON_NO_OPEN opt out
    rationale: 'Founder: seamless; Aegis: keep the token off argv'
  - id: D-ws-sfs
    decision: A WebSocket upgrade with no Sec-Fetch-Site is accepted on the exact Origin; HTTP non-static routes still require the header
    rationale: Chrome sends no Fetch Metadata on the WS handshake; Origin is always sent and is exact-locked
learnings:
  - A GUI-pin embed made inside a worktree is wrong for CI (esbuild writes a different path comment); re-embed from the main checkout, or symlink the worktree's node_modules packages
  - Linux reuses inodes immediately; never identify a lock file by inode alone; use a nonce
  - No test loaded a real browser, so the blank page reached the founder; a headless-Chrome smoke test is needed (T-006 item 6)
  - Builders hit the 50-turn limit repeatedly; resume them with SendMessage and tight budgets
